WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.770
You touch a hot pan.

2
00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:05.390
Before you've had time to think,
your hand has jerked away.

3
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:07.270
You didn't decide to move it.

4
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.930
Nobody gave the order.

5
00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:12.710
So how can your body act before
you've made up your mind?

6
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.370
In this mission, you'll follow
a nerve impulse from a receptor,

7
00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.610
along a sensory neurone,
through a neurone in between,

8
00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.220
and out along a motor
neurone to a muscle.

9
00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:26.170
You'll find out what makes
a reflex fast and automatic.

10
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:29.530
And you'll see how a signal
crosses the tiny gaps between

11
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.850
neurones, called synapses.

12
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.170
Your mission: explain how your
hand moves before you think.
